WEBVTT

00:00:52.560 --> 00:00:54.320
MALE FISH: Wow.
FEMALE FISH: Mmm.

00:00:55.760 --> 00:00:57.600
-Wow.
-Mmm-hmm.

00:00:59.320 --> 00:01:00.880
-Wow.
-Yes, Marlin.

00:01:00.960 --> 00:01:03.040
I see it. It's beautiful.

00:01:03.120 --> 00:01:05.800
So, Coral, when you said
you wanted an ocean view,

00:01:05.880 --> 00:01:09.600
you didn't think you were going
to get the whole ocean, did you?

00:01:11.400 --> 00:01:12.560
Oh, yeah!

00:01:12.640 --> 00:01:16.720
A fish can breathe out here.
Did your man deliver or did he deliver?

00:01:16.800 --> 00:01:19.240
-My man delivered.
-It wasn't so easy.

00:01:19.320 --> 00:01:22.200
A lot of clownfish
had their eyes on this place.

00:01:22.280 --> 00:01:25.960
You better believe they did.
Every single one of them.

00:01:26.040 --> 00:01:29.280
You did good
and the neighborhood is awesome.

00:01:29.960 --> 00:01:31.960
(LAUGHTER OF YOUNG FISH)

00:01:39.720 --> 00:01:44.720
-So you do like it, don't you?
-No, no, I really do like it.

00:01:44.800 --> 00:01:47.800
But, Marlin, I know that
the Drop Off is desirable,

00:01:47.920 --> 00:01:49.800
great schools, amazing view,

00:01:49.920 --> 00:01:52.400
but do we really need so much space?

00:01:52.480 --> 00:01:55.040
Coral, honey,
these are our kids we're talking about.

00:01:55.120 --> 00:01:56.240
They deserve the best.

00:01:56.320 --> 00:02:00.640
Look. They'll wake up, poke their
little heads out and see a whale

00:02:01.040 --> 00:02:02.840
-right by their bedroom window!
-Shh!

00:02:03.280 --> 00:02:06.480
-You're going to wake the kids.
-Oh, right. Right.

00:02:10.160 --> 00:02:11.480
Aw, look.

00:02:12.920 --> 00:02:14.840
They're dreaming.

00:02:15.720 --> 00:02:19.320
-We still have to name them.
-All of them? Right now?

00:02:19.400 --> 00:02:22.560
All right. We'll name this half Marlin Jr.

00:02:22.640 --> 00:02:24.760
and this half Coral Jr.

00:02:24.840 --> 00:02:27.280
-Okay, we're done.
-I like Nemo.

00:02:27.360 --> 00:02:28.760
Nemo?

00:02:28.840 --> 00:02:32.680
We'll name one Nemo,
but I'd like most of them to be Marlin Jr.

00:02:32.760 --> 00:02:35.680
In a couple of days,
we're going to be parents!

00:02:35.760 --> 00:02:36.920
Yeah.

00:02:38.040 --> 00:02:40.520
-What if they don't like me?
-Marlin...

00:02:40.880 --> 00:02:42.280
There's over 400 eggs.

00:02:42.360 --> 00:02:45.600
Odds are one of them
is bound to like you.

00:02:48.880 --> 00:02:49.920
What?

00:02:50.640 --> 00:02:53.360
-You remember how we met?
-I try not to.

00:02:53.440 --> 00:02:54.640
Well, I remember.

00:02:54.720 --> 00:02:57.560
Excuse me, miss.
Can you see if I have a hook in my lip?

00:02:57.640 --> 00:02:59.840
-Marlin.
-Look closer.

00:02:59.920 --> 00:03:03.120
-CORAL: (LAUGHS) Get away!
-Here he is. Cutie's here!

00:03:05.520 --> 00:03:07.400
Where did everybody go?

00:03:14.360 --> 00:03:16.040
Coral, get inside the house.

00:03:18.320 --> 00:03:21.000
No, don't. They'll be fine.
Just get inside.

00:03:21.080 --> 00:03:22.760
You. Right now.

00:03:25.400 --> 00:03:26.760
No!

00:03:39.960 --> 00:03:41.440
(MARLIN GROANS)

00:03:45.960 --> 00:03:47.000
Coral!

00:03:53.440 --> 00:03:54.600
Coral?

00:03:57.000 --> 00:03:58.320
Coral?

00:04:01.200 --> 00:04:02.200
(GASPS)

00:04:05.200 --> 00:04:06.480
Coral!

00:04:09.040 --> 00:04:10.360
Coral!

00:04:16.280 --> 00:04:17.640
Coral?

00:04:40.520 --> 00:04:42.560
There, there.

00:04:42.640 --> 00:04:44.840
It's okay. Daddy's here.

00:04:46.160 --> 00:04:47.880
Daddy's got you.

00:04:50.960 --> 00:04:55.120
I promise I will never let
anything happen to you,

00:04:55.200 --> 00:04:56.520
Nemo.

